hadiths[188]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who visits the sick is in the fruit-gathering garden of Paradise, and when he sits with him, mercy covers him."""
"3964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who visits the sick walks in the fruit-gathering garden of Paradise until he returns."""
"3965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Aishah is my wife in Paradise."""
"3966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shows enmity to Ali, Allah shows enmity to him."""
"3967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A borrowed item is to be returned."""
"3968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ashura is the day of the tenth."""
"3969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Treat her with the Book of Allah."""
"3970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Most of the people of Hell are women."""
"3971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine."""
"3972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! You must straighten your rows, or else Allah will cause division between your faces."""
"3973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Allah has removed hardship from the religion, except for a person who unjustly attacks the honour of another man; it is he who will fall into hardship and be ruined. O servants of Allah! Seek treatment, for Allah Almighty has not created any disease without placing a cure for it, except for one disease: old age."""
"3974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship during times of turmoil and tribulation is like emigrating to me."""
"3975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abdullah bin Salam is the tenth of ten in Paradise."""
"3976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Freeing a slave (itq al-nasamah) is that you alone free him, and releasing a neck (fakk al-raqabah) is that you help in freeing him."""
"3977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Uthman revived my Ummah."""
"3978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Uthman is very modest; even the angels feel shy before him."""
"3979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Uthman is in Paradise."""
"3980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How wonderful is the affair of the believer! All of his affairs are good for him, and this is not the case for anyone except the believer. If something pleasing befalls him, he gives thanks, and that is good for him; and if hardship befalls him, he is patient, and that too is good for him."""
"3981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our Lord marvels at a man who fights in the path of Allah, then his companions flee, but knowing his duty he returns until his blood is shed. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to His angels: 'Look at My servant! He returned out of longing for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me, until his blood was shed.'"""
"3982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our Lord marvels at people who are led to Paradise in chains."""
"3983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I marvelled at people who are being driven to Paradise in chains while they are unwilling."""
"3984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I marvel at the patience and generosity of my brother Yusuf, may Allah forgive him: when a messenger was sent to him to seek his interpretation of the dream, had it been me, I would not have done so until I was released from prison. And I marvel at his patience and generosity, may Allah forgive him: when they came to release him, he did not come out until he had informed them of his justification; had it been me, I would have hastened. And had it not been for that word, he would not have remained in prison for so long, where he sought release from other than Allah."""
"3985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I marvel at the believer: Allah Almighty does not decree anything for him except that it is good for him."""
"3986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I marvel at the Muslim: when a calamity befalls him, he hopes for reward and is patient, and when good befalls him, he praises Allah and gives thanks. Indeed, the Muslim is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."""
"3987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I marvel at people of my Ummah who will ride the sea like kings upon thrones."""
"3988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O you who prays, you have been hasty! When you pray and sit, first praise Allah as He deserves, then send blessings upon me, then supplicate to Him."""
"3989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to break the fast and delay the pre-dawn meal (suhur)."""
"3990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to set out for Makkah, for none of you knows what illness or need may befall him."""
"3991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The number of the vessels of the Pond is like the number of the stars in the sky."""
"3992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The punishment of the grave is true."""
"3993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The punishment of my Ummah will take place in this world."""
"3994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The punishment of this Ummah has been placed in its own hands, in its worldly life."""
"3995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman was punished because of a cat which she kept confined until it died of hunger, and because of it she entered the Fire. Allah said: 'You neither fed it nor gave it drink when you confined it, nor did you set it free so that it could eat from the insects of the earth.'"""
"3996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman was punished because of a cat; she kept it tied up until it died, and she did not release it so that it could eat from the insects and creatures of the earth, so Hell became due for her because of that."""
"3997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was taken up until I reached a height where I heard the scratching of the pens."""
"3998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A shelter like the shelter of Musa."""
"3999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The nations were shown to me, and I saw a prophet with a small group, a prophet with one or two men, and a prophet with no one at all. Then a huge multitude appeared before me and I thought that they were my Ummah, but I was told: This is Musa and his people. But look towards the horizon; and there was a huge multitude. Then I was told: Look towards the other horizon; and there too was a huge multitude. Then I was told: This is your Ummah, and with them are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment. They are those who do not perform ruqyah, nor ask for ruqyah, nor take evil omens, nor have themselves cauterised, and who put their trust in their Lord."""
"4000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The days were shown to me, and among them Friday was shown to me. It was like a white mirror, and in its middle was a black spot. I asked: What is this? It was said: The Hour."""
"4001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise was shown to me, so much so that had I stretched out my hand I would have taken some of its clusters of fruit. And Hell was shown to me, and I began to blow, fearing that its heat would envelop you. In it I saw the one who stole the sacrificial camel of the Messenger of Allah, and in it I saw the brother of Banu Da'da', who used to steal the belongings of the pilgrims; when he was caught, he would say: This is the work of my hooked staff. And in it I saw a tall black woman being punished because of a cat: she kept it tied up, neither fed it nor gave it water, nor let it go so that it could eat from the insects and creatures of the earth, until it died. And indeed the sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death or the life of anyone; rather, they are two of the signs of Allah. So when either of them is eclipsed, hasten to the remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"4002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just now Paradise and Hell were shown to me beyond this wall. I have never seen good and evil as I have today. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."""
"4003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah was shown to me with its deeds, both good and bad. Among its good deeds I saw the removal of something harmful from the road, and among its bad deeds I saw spittle in the mosque that had not been buried."""
"4004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prophets were shown to me. Musa was a lean man, as though he were one of the men of Shanu'ah. I saw Isa bin Maryam, and the person I have seen who most resembles him is Urwah bin Mas'ud. I saw Ibrahim, and the person I have seen who most resembles him is your companion - meaning himself (peace and blessings be upon him). And I saw Jibril, and the person I have seen who most resembles him is Dihyah."""
"4005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole of Arafah is a place of standing."""
"4006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole of Arafah is a place of standing, and keep away from the valley of Uranah; the whole of Muzdalifah is a place of standing, and keep away from the valley of Muhassir; and the whole of Mina is a place of sacrifice."""
"4007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Build a shelter like the shelter of Musa, of a little grass and some pieces of wood, for the matter is coming sooner than that."""
"4008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps a man speaks about what takes place between him and his wife, or perhaps a woman speaks about what takes place between her and her husband. Do not do so, for the likeness of that is the likeness of a male devil who met a female devil on the road and had intercourse with her while people were watching."""
"4009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ten things are part of the fitrah (natural disposition): trimming the moustache, letting the beard grow, using the siwak, drawing water into the nose, clipping the nails, washing the finger joints, plucking the armpit hair, shaving the pubic hair, and cleaning oneself with water after relieving oneself."""
"4010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ten people are in Paradise: the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, Az-Zubayr bin al-Awwam is in Paradise, Sa'd bin Malik is in Paradise, Abdur-Rahman bin Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'id bin Zayd is in Paradise."""
"4011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A band of Muslims will conquer the White Palace, that is, the palace of Kisra."""
"4012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two groups of my Ummah Allah has protected from Hell: a group that will wage jihad in India (Hind), and a group that will be with Isa bin Maryam."""
"4013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatness of the reward comes with the greatness of the affliction, and when Allah loves a people He tests them."""
"4014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The central home of Islam is in Sham."""
"4015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money of the dhimmis (non-Muslim protected citizens) is half the blood money of the Muslims."""
"4016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money for quasi-deliberate killing is heavy like the blood money for deliberate killing, but the one who commits it is not killed."""
"4017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The punishment of this Ummah will be by the sword."""
"4018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why do you press your children's throats with this 'ilaq?! You should use this Indian wood (aloeswood), for in it is a cure for seven diseases, among them pleurisy. It is put into the nose for 'udhrah (throat inflammation), and poured into one side of the mouth for pleurisy."""
"4019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why do you gesture with your hands as though they were the tails of restive horses?! It is enough for any of you to place his hand on his thigh and then give salam to his brother on his right and his left."""
"4020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why would one of you kill his brother? When one of you sees something in his brother that pleases him, let him pray for blessing for him."""
"4021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it."""
"4022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it, for it is a means of discipline for them."""
"4023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Knowledge that is not spoken of is like a treasure from which nothing is spent."""
"4024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Knowledge that does not benefit is like a treasure from which nothing is spent."""
"4025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Teach the child the prayer at the age of seven, and beat him for it at the age of ten."""
"4026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Teach your children the prayer when they reach seven years, beat them for it when they reach ten years, and separate their beds."""
"4027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Teach, make things easy and do not make them difficult, give glad tidings and do not drive people away; and when one of you becomes angry, let him remain silent."""
"4028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Teach Hafsah the ruqyah for namlah (skin sores)."""
"4029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the entrances of Madinah there are angels standing guard; neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it."""
"4030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the hump of every camel there is a devil, so subdue them by riding them, for in reality it is Allah Almighty who carries."""
"4031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the back of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, mention the name of Allah, and then do not fall short in fulfilling your needs."""
"4032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At every door of the mosque there are two angels who record those who come, the first and then the next. The one who came first is like one who offers a camel in sacrifice, the one who came after him is like one who offers a cow, the one who came after him is like one who offers a goat, the one who came after him is like one who offers a bird, and the one who came after him is like one who offers an egg. Then when the imam sits, the angels roll up the scrolls."""
"4033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Upon every clan lies the responsibility for blood money."""
"4034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is upon every Muslim man to take a ritual bath (ghusl) on one day in every seven days, and that is Friday."""
"4035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Upon every joint of the son of Adam there is a charity every day, and two rak'ahs of the Duha (forenoon) prayer suffice for all of that."""
"4036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going to the Friday prayer is obligatory upon everyone who has reached puberty, and the ritual bath (ghusl) is obligatory upon everyone who goes to the Friday prayer."""
"4037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Upon every Muslim there is charity. If he finds nothing, let him work with his hand, benefit himself and give charity. If he is not able to, let him help someone in need who is in distress. If he cannot do this either, let him enjoin good. And if he does not do this either, let him refrain from evil, for that too is charity for him."""
"4038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Upon every soul, on every day on which the sun rises, there is a charity from himself upon himself. Among the doors of charity are: saying the takbir, saying 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), saying 'Alhamdu lillah' (Praise be to Allah), saying 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no deity but Allah), saying 'Astaghfirullah' (I seek the forgiveness of Allah), enjoining good, forbidding evil, removing thorns, bones and stones from the people's path, guiding the blind, making the deaf and the mute hear by signs until they understand, showing someone who asks the way to the place of his need which you know, running swiftly on your legs to the distressed person who is calling for help, and exerting the strength of your arms in helping the weak. All of these are doors of charity from you upon yourself. And in your intercourse with your wife there is also a reward for you. Tell me, if you had a son who reached adulthood and you hoped for his reward, and then he died, would you not count him as a source of reward? Did you create him? Did you guide him? Did you provide for him? In the same way, place your seed in what is lawful for it and keep it away from what is unlawful; then if Allah wills He gives it life, and if He wills He causes it to die, and you still have a reward."""
"4039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory upon you to listen and obey, in your hardship and your ease, in what you like and what you dislike, and even when others are given preference over you."""
"4040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to horses, for goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."""
"4041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt gentleness, for gentleness is not in anything except that it beautifies it, and it is not removed from anything except that it disfigures it."""
"4042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt gentleness, and beware of harshness and obscenity."""
"4043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform tayammum with the earth, for it is sufficient for you."""
"4044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to fasting, for there is no deed like it."""
"4045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to emigration (hijrah), for there is no deed like it. Hold fast to jihad, for there is no deed like it. Hold fast to fasting, for there is no deed like it. Hold fast to prostration, for you will not make any prostration for Allah except that Allah will raise you a degree by it and remove a sin from you by it."""
"4046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt the fear (taqwa) of Allah Almighty, and say the takbir whenever you climb any height."""
"4047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to comprehensive and concise supplications. Say: O Allah, I ask You for all good, the immediate and the delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know; and I seek refuge in You from all evil, the immediate and the delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know; and I ask You for Paradise and for every word and deed that brings one near to it; and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and from every word and deed that brings one near to it; and I ask You for what Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from what Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sought refuge in You from; and whatever decree You have decreed for me, make its outcome one of right guidance."""
"4048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to good character and much silence. By the One in whose hand is my soul, creation has not adorned itself with anything like these two."""
"4049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to speaking well and feeding others."""
"4050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to prostrating much, for you will not make any prostration for Allah except that Allah will raise you a degree by it and remove a sin from you by it."""
"4051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to those leather waterskins whose mouths are tied."""
"4052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to doing good, for it saves from an evil death; and hold fast to secret charity, for it extinguishes the anger of the Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"4053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to marrying virgins, for they have sweeter mouths, more fertile wombs, are warmer in passion, and are more content with little effort."""
"4054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to applying kohl (ithmid) at the time of sleep, for it clears the eyesight and grows the hair."""
"4055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to applying kohl (ithmid), for it grows the hair, removes impurities from the eye and clears the eyesight."""
"4056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to applying kohl (ithmid), for it clears the eyesight and grows the hair."""
"4057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care of (that is, kill) the pitch-black (dog) with two spots, for it is a devil."""
"4058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to marriage; and whoever is not able to, let him fast, for it is a restraint for him (breaking his desire)."""
"4059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to cow's milk, for the cow grazes on every kind of tree, and it is a cure for every disease."""
"4060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to cow's milk, for it is a medicine, and to its fat, for it is a cure; and beware of its meat, for its meat is a disease."""
"4061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to cow's milk, for it is a cure, and its ghee is a medicine, and its meat is a disease."""
"4062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to white clothes; let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them, for they are the best of your clothes."""
"4063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to jihad in the path of Allah, for it is one of the gates of Paradise; through it Allah removes grief and anxiety."""
"4064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to travelling by night, for the earth is traversed more quickly at night."""
"4065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to archery, for it is the best of your games."""
"4066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to archery, for it is the best of your pastimes."""
"4067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to sana (senna) and sanut, for in them both is a cure for every disease except sam, and that is death."""
"4068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to the tooth-stick (miswak), for it purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."""
"4069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to Sham (Syria)."""
"4070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to Sham (Syria), for it is the choicest of Allah's lands, and the chosen ones of His creation dwell in it. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its pools, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has guaranteed to me Sham and its people."""
"4071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise; and a man keeps speaking the truth and striving for truthfulness until he is written with Allah as a siddiq (truthful one). And beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to Hell; and a man keeps lying and striving for lying until he is written with Allah as a kadhdhab (liar)."""
"4072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and both of them are in Paradise; and beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both of them are in Hell. Ask Allah for certainty and well-being, for no one has been given, after certainty, anything better than well-being. Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not cut off relations with one another and do not turn your backs on one another; and, O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another as Allah has commanded you."""
"4073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to sheep and goats, for they are among the animals of Paradise; pray in their pens and wipe the dirt from their noses."""
"4074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to white clothes; let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."""
"4075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to white clothes; wear them and shroud your dead in them."""
"4076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to small pebbles, the kind with which the Jamrah is stoned."""
"4077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Act upon the concession of Allah which He has granted you."""
"4078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to marrying young women, for they have purer mouths, more fertile wombs and are warmer in passion."""
"4079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to the night prayer (qiyam al-layl), for it was the practice of the righteous before you, a means of nearness to Allah Almighty, a restraint from sin, an expiation for evil deeds, and a means of driving disease away from the body."""
"4080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to the meat of the back, for it is among the best of it."""
"4081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to this pre-dawn meal (suhur), for it is the blessed morning meal."""
"4082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to this Indian wood (costus), for in it are cures for seven diseases: it is put into the nose for tonsillitis ('udhrah), and poured into one side of the mouth for pleurisy (dhat al-janb)."""
"4083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to this black seed, for in it is a cure for every disease except sam, and that is death."""
"4084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to offering this prayer in your homes"" - meaning the sunnah prayer after Maghrib."
"4085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do only those deeds which you are able to, for Allah does not tire of rewarding until you yourselves tire of doing deeds."""
"4086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt a moderate way, for whoever is harsh with this religion, it will overpower him."""
"4087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to tasbih, tahlil and taqdis (glorifying, declaring the Oneness and the holiness of Allah), and count them on your fingertips, for they will be questioned and made to speak. And do not be heedless, lest you forget the mercy."""
"4088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Upon them is what they were charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with."""
"4089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am the mawla (patron) of, Ali bin Abi Talib is his mawla."""
"4090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ali is to me in the position that Harun (Aaron) was to Musa (Moses), except that there is no prophet after me."""
"4091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ali is from me and I am from Ali, and no one will convey on my behalf except myself or Ali."""
"4092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ali will pay off my debt."""
"4093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umar, I did it deliberately."""
"4094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lifespans of my Ummah are between sixty and seventy years."""
"4095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Amr bin al-As is among the righteous people of Quraysh."""
"4096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The flourishing of Bayt al-Maqdis is a sign of the ruin of Yathrib, the ruin of Yathrib is a sign of the outbreak of the great battle, the outbreak of the great battle is a sign of the conquest of Constantinople, and the conquest of Constantinople is a sign of the emergence of the Dajjal."""
"4097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Performing Umrah in Ramadan is equal to Hajj."""
"4098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Performing Umrah in Ramadan is equal to performing Hajj with me."""
"4099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This man did little, yet he was rewarded greatly."""
"4100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's paternal uncle is like his father."""
"4101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ammar will be killed by the rebellious group."""
"4102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever two matters were put before Ammar, he always chose the more correct of the two."""
"4103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ammar is filled with faith right down to the joints of his bones."""
"4104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abbas is my paternal uncle and is like my father."""
"4105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a boy, two goats of equal age, and for a girl, one goat."""
"4106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a boy, two goats, and for a girl, one goat; it does not harm you whether they are male or female."""
"4107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a boy, two aqiqahs, and for a girl, one aqiqah."""
"4108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""With Allah are the treasuries of good and evil, and their keys are certain men. So glad tidings to the one whom Allah has made a key to good and a lock against evil, and woe to the one whom Allah has made a key to evil and a lock against good."""
"4109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Visit the sick and follow the funeral processions; they remind you of the Hereafter."""
"4110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell, seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal), and seek refuge with Allah from the trials of life and death."""
"4111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two eyes will not see the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night keeping guard in the path of Allah."""
"4112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two eyes will not be touched by the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night keeping guard in the path of Allah."""
"4113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two eyes will never be touched by the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night keeping guard in the path of Allah."""
"4114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back the gift he has given is like one who eats his own vomit back."""
"4115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A borrowed item ('ariyah) is to be returned, and a lent gift (minhah) is to be given back."""
"4116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A borrowed item ('ariyah) is to be returned, a lent gift (minhah) is to be given back, a debt is to be paid, and the guarantor is liable for what he has taken on."""
"4117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who works on collecting charity with justice is like one who fights in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, until he returns to his home."""
"4118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The servants are the servants of Allah and the lands are the lands of Allah. So whoever brings any part of dead land to life, it is his, and an unjust root has no right."""
"4119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship in times of turmoil and strife is equal to migrating to me."""
"4120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abbas is the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and a man's paternal uncle is like his father."""
"4121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of a runaway slave is not accepted until he returns to his masters."""
"4122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'atirah is a right."""
"4123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is strange is that some people of my Ummah will head for the House (the Ka'bah) after a man from Quraysh who will have sought refuge in the House, until, when they reach the plain of al-Bayda', they will be swallowed up by the earth. Among them will be one who came knowingly, one who was brought by force, and the wayfarer; they will all perish in a single destruction, but they will depart to different destinations, and Allah will raise them according to their intentions."""
"4124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An injury caused by an animal carries no liability, a well carries no liability, a mine carries no liability, and on buried treasure (rikaz) there is one-fifth."""
"4125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An injury caused by an animal carries no liability, and a mine carries no liability."""
"4126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ajwah date is from Paradise, and in it is a cure for poison; and the truffle is from the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."""
"4127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ajwah date is from Paradise, and in it is a cure for poison; and the truffle is from the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."""
"4128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leadership: its beginning is blame, its end is regret, and then punishment on the Day of Resurrection."""
"4129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Usaylah means sexual intercourse."""
"4130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sneezing is from Allah and yawning is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for if he says 'aah, aah', Satan laughs from inside his belly. And indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, loves sneezing and dislikes yawning."""
"4131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blood money is the responsibility of the paternal male relatives ('asabah), and for a stillborn fetus the compensation is a male or female slave."""
"4132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The aqiqah is slaughtered on the seventh, fourteenth or twenty-first day."""
"4133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The aqiqah is a right: for a boy, two goats of equal age, and for a girl, one goat."""
"4134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In deliberate killing there is retaliation (qisas), and in accidental killing there is blood money."""
"4135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One Umrah to the next is an expiation for the sins and wrongdoings committed between them, and an accepted Hajj (Hajj mabrur) has no reward except Paradise."""
"4136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One Umrah to the next is an expiation for the sins committed between them, and an accepted Hajj (Hajj mabrur) has no reward except Paradise."""
"4137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'umra (a lifetime grant) is valid for those to whom it is given."""
"4138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'umra (a lifetime grant) is valid for those to whom it is given, and the ruqba is likewise valid for those to whom it is given."""
"4139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'umra is valid for the one to whom it is granted, and the ruqba is valid for the one to whom it is granted; and the one who takes back his gift is like one who takes back his own vomit."""
"4140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'umra belongs to the one to whom it has been given."""
"4141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The 'umra is an inheritance for those to whom it is given."""
"4142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The paternal uncle is like a father."""
"4143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The covenant between us and them is the prayer; so whoever abandons it has committed disbelief."""
"4144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil eye brings a man to the grave and brings a camel to the cooking pot."""
"4145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil eye is real."""
"4146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil eye is real; it brings a person down from a height."""
"4147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil eye is real, and if anything could outstrip destiny, the evil eye would outstrip it. And when you are asked to wash, then wash."""
"4148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The eye is the drawstring of the buttocks, so when the eye sleeps, the drawstring is loosened."""
"4149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The eye is the drawstring of the buttocks, so whoever sleeps should perform ablution (wudu)."""
"4150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery."""
